07:51.160 --> 07:53.830
We know that the real L of t,
whatever we used to approximate

07:53.830 --> 07:56.590
it, it's not going to have
these sharp edges because

07:56.590 --> 07:57.660
it's differentiable.

07:57.660 --> 07:58.660
It's actually twice
differentiable.

07:58.660 --> 08:01.460
So it's actually going to be
a smoother curve, right?

08:01.460 --> 08:02.790
Because we can take the
